NNAAMMEE
     ddooaass — execute commands as another user

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ddooaass [--LLnnss] [--aa _s_t_y_l_e] [--CC _c_o_n_f_i_g] [--uu _u_s_e_r] _c_o_m_m_a_n_d [_a_r_g _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddooaass utility executes the given command as another user.  The _c_o_m_m_a_n_d
     argument is mandatory unless --CC, --LL, or --ss is specified.

     The user will be required to authenticate by entering their password, un‐
     less configured otherwise.

     By default, a new environment is created.  The variables HOME, LOGNAME,
     PATH, SHELL, and USER and the umask(2) are set to values appropriate for
     the target user.  DOAS_USER is set to the name of the user executing
     ddooaass.  The variables DISPLAY and TERM are inherited from the current en‐
     vironment.  This behavior may be modified by the config file.  The work‐
     ing directory is not changed.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa _s_t_y_l_e    Use the specified authentication style when validating the
                 user, as allowed by _/_e_t_c_/_l_o_g_i_n_._c_o_n_f.  A list of doas-specific
                 authentication methods may be configured by adding an
                 ‘auth-doas’ entry in login.conf(5).

     --CC _c_o_n_f_i_g   Parse and check the configuration file _c_o_n_f_i_g, then exit.  If
                 _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is supplied, ddooaass will also perform command matching.
                 In the latter case either ‘permit’, ‘permit nopass’ or ‘deny’
                 will be printed on standard output, depending on command
                 matching results.  No command is executed.

     --LL          Clear any persisted authentications from previous invoca‐
                 tions, then immediately exit.  No command is executed.

     --nn          Non interactive mode, fail if the matching rule doesn't have
                 the nnooppaassss option.

     --ss          Execute the shell from SHELL or _/_e_t_c_/_p_a_s_s_w_d.

     --uu _u_s_e_r     Execute the command as _u_s_e_r.  The default is root.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ddooaass utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.  It may
     fail for one of the following reasons:

     ••   The config file _/_e_t_c_/_d_o_a_s_._c_o_n_f could not be parsed.
     ••   The user attempted to run a command which is not permitted.
     ••   The password was incorrect.
     ••   The specified command was not found or is not executable.

